{
  "id": "y9-algorithms-l8",
  "label": "9CT.01 L8: Nested Iteration - Plant a Whole Grid",
  "steps": [
    {"id":"do-now","label":"Do Now: Iteration Retrieval","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l8-do-now","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l8_do_now","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Iteration Retrieval</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Quick recall from last lesson.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l8-do-now-a\">(a) What instruction ends a FOR loop?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-do-now-a\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-do-now-a\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l8-do-now-b\">(b) FOR Count &lt;- 1 TO 5 - how many times does the loop run?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-do-now-b\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-do-now-b\"></div></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-do-now-check\">Check answers</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-do-now-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div>"},
    {"id":"title","label":"Nested Iteration: Plant a Whole Grid","content":"<div class=\"lesson-title-slide\"><p class=\"lesson-title-kicker\">Algorithms and Data</p><h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Nested Iteration: Plant a Whole Grid</h2><p>Year 9, 9CT.01</p></div>"},
    {"id":"objectives","label":"Three Goals","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Three Goals</h2><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Nest</h3><p>Put one FOR loop completely inside another.</p></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Track</h3><p>Follow two loop variables changing at the same time.</p></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Multiply</h3><p>Work out the total number of passes: rows times columns.</p></div></div>"},
    {"id":"direct-instruction","label":"Nested FOR Syntax","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Nested FOR Syntax</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A Strip Farm plants one row. A Grid Farm plants several rows, by putting one FOR loop <strong>inside</strong> another.</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">FOR Row &lt;- 0 TO 1</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;FOR Col &lt;- 0 TO 2</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CALL SetPosition(Col, Row)</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CALL Buy(&quot;Carrot&quot;)</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CALL Plant(&quot;Carrot&quot;)</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;NEXT Col</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">NEXT Row</div></div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>The <strong>inner</strong> loop (Col) runs all the way through for every single pass of the <strong>outer</strong> loop (Row).</li><li>Indent the inner loop one level further, so the nesting is visible.</li><li>Each inner loop must close with its own NEXT before the outer loop's NEXT.</li><li>Total passes = outer passes &times; inner passes.</li></ul>"},
    {"id":"worked-check","label":"Check: Trace the Grid","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l8-worked-check","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l8_worked_check","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check: Trace the Grid</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Look at the nested loop again: <code>FOR Row &lt;- 0 TO 1</code> around <code>FOR Col &lt;- 0 TO 2</code>.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l8-worked-check-a\">(a) How many times does the outer loop (Row) run?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-worked-check-a\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-worked-check-a\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l8-worked-check-b\">(b) So how many times does CALL Plant run in total?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-worked-check-b\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-worked-check-b\"></div></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-worked-check-button\">Check answers</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-worked-check-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div>"},
    {"id":"farmer-tutorial","label":"Machine Tutorial: Grid Farm","type":"app-link","buttonId":"y9-algorithms-l8-farmer-button","appId":"pseudocodefarmer","appQuery":"tutorial=grid-farm","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Machine Tutorial: Grid Farm</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Open Pseudocode Farmer. It will take you straight into the Grid Farm tutorial - follow every step in order.</p><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Complete when</h3><p>The tutorial panel says &quot;Tutorial complete&quot; and six Carrots are planted in a 3-wide, 2-deep block from a single Run.</p></div><div class=\"lesson-app-link\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-farmer-button\">Open Pseudocode Farmer</button></div>"},
    {"id":"scaffold-fill-blank","label":"Fix the Grid Size","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l8-fill-blank","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l8_fill_blank","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Fix the Grid Size</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">This is meant to plant a grid of 8 Potatoes (2 rows of 4), but it only plants 6.</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">FOR Row &lt;- 0 TO 1</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;FOR Col &lt;- 0 TO 2</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CALL SetPosition(Col, Row)</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CALL Buy(&quot;Potato&quot;)</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CALL Plant(&quot;Potato&quot;)</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;NEXT Col</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">NEXT Row</div></div><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l8-fill-blank-a\">Rewrite the inner FOR line only, so the grid becomes 2 rows of 4 (8 Potatoes total).</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-fill-blank-a\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-fill-blank-a\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-fill-blank-button\">Check answer</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-fill-blank-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div>"},
    {"id":"independent-task","label":"Independent Task: Three by Two","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l8-independent","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l8_independent","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Independent Task: Three by Two</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Write your own nested FOR loops from scratch. No walkthrough this time.</p><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Requirement</h3><p>Using the loop variables <code>Row</code> and <code>Col</code>, buy and plant Tomato seeds in a grid of 3 rows and 2 columns (6 total).</p></div><div class=\"pseudocode-check\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l8-independent-code\"><strong>Your nested loops</strong></label><textarea id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-independent-code\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-independent-code\" spellcheck=\"false\" rows=\"7\"></textarea><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-independent-check\">Check my answer</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-independent-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div></div>"},
    {"id":"plenary","label":"Plenary: Nested Iteration","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y9-algorithms-l8-plenary","validatorKey":"y9_algorithms_l8_plenary","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Nested Iteration</h2><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l8-plenary-a\">(a) FOR A &lt;- 1 TO 3 contains FOR B &lt;- 1 TO 4. How many total passes of the inner loop happen?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-plenary-a\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-plenary-a\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y9-algorithms-l8-plenary-b\">(b) Why must the inner loop's NEXT come before the outer loop's NEXT?</label><input id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-plenary-b\" class=\"lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-plenary-b\"></div></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-plenary-button\">Check answers</button><div id=\"y9-algorithms-l8-plenary-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\"></div><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Next lesson: <strong>Arrays</strong> - storing a list of exact spots to farm.</p>"}
  ],
  "validators": {
    "y9_algorithms_l8_do_now":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*next\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"A FOR loop ends with NEXT and the loop variable's name."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*5\\s*(?:times)?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"1 TO 5 counts 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 - five passes."}],
    "y9_algorithms_l8_worked_check":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*2\\s*(?:times)?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"0 TO 1 gives two passes: 0, then 1."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*6\\s*(?:times)?\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"2 outer passes x 3 inner passes = 6 total."}],
    "y9_algorithms_l8_fill_blank":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"for\\s*col\\s*(?:<-|←)\\s*0\\s*to\\s*3","flags":"i"},"feedback":"4 columns means Col needs 4 values: 0, 1, 2, 3 - so change TO 2 to TO 3."}],
    "y9_algorithms_l8_independent":[{"suffix":"code","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"for\\s*row\\s*(?:<-|←)\\s*0\\s*to\\s*2[\\s\\S]*?for\\s*col\\s*(?:<-|←)\\s*0\\s*to\\s*1[\\s\\S]*?call\\s*buy\\s*\\(\\s*[\"']tomato[\"']\\s*\\)[\\s\\S]*?call\\s*plant\\s*\\(\\s*[\"']tomato[\"']\\s*\\)[\\s\\S]*?next\\s*col[\\s\\S]*?next\\s*row","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Check the dimensions (3 rows means TO 2 for Row, 2 columns means TO 1 for Col), the crop (Tomato), and that Col's NEXT comes before Row's NEXT."}],
    "y9_algorithms_l8_plenary":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*12\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"3 outer passes x 4 inner passes = 12."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"(?=.*(?:finish|complete|close|before|inside)).*","flags":"i"},"feedback":"The inner loop must fully finish (all its passes) before the outer loop can move to its next pass."}]
  }
}
